{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Sync Implementation Progress to ClickUp",
  "description": "Analyzes the current state of the codebase against the ClickUp tasks in the \"Implementar plataforma\" milestone and posts progress comments on each matching task. Covers all 6 epics (ÉPICA 0–5) and their user stories (US/NFR). Triggered manually.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You must analyze the current implementation status of this repository and compare it against the ClickUp tasks in the \"Implementar plataforma\" milestone (task ID: 86afu5ga8) under the \"Implementación del Prototipo\" list.\n\n## ClickUp Task Map\n\nBelow is the full task tree. Each entry has a ClickUp task ID and a user story / NFR name.\n\n### ÉPICA 0 – Requerimientos transversales (86afu5k8w)\n- US-AUT-01 - Registro de usuario arrendatario (86afwygv0)\n- US-AUT-02 - Registro de usuario arrendador (86afwyguv)\n- US-AUT-03 - Inicio de sesión (86afwygux)\n- NFR-01 – Mobile-first y correcto funcionamiento en celular (86afu5ke9)\n- NFR-02 – Baja carga cognitiva en la interfaz (86afu5kee)\n- NFR-03 – Claridad explicativa en cada paso (86afu5kea)\n- NFR-04 – Retroalimentación visible ante errores (86afu5kec)\n- NFR-05 – Diseño accesible y legible (86afu5ked)\n- NFR-06 – Generar confianza en pagos y firma digital (86afu5keb)\n\n### ÉPICA 1 – Exploración de oferta (86afu5k8x)\n- US-01 – Buscar inmuebles (86afu5kew)\n- US-02 – Filtrar por zona/barrio (86afu5keq)\n- US-03 – Ver fotos obligatorias (86afu5kef)\n- US-04 – Ver fecha de publicación (86afu5kep)\n- US-05 – Contactar al arrendador (86afu5keu)\n\n### ÉPICA 2 – Gestión de publicación (86afu5k90)\n- US-06 – Crear publicación básica (86afu5kek)\n- US-07 – Cargar fotos obligatorias (86afu5ken)\n- US-08 – Publicar desde el celular (86afu5keh)\n- US-09 – Recibir notificaciones de interesados (86afu5ket)\n\n### ÉPICA 3 – Gestión de contrato (86afu5k8z)\n- US-10 – Cargar contrato (86afu5kez)\n- US-11 – Ver resumen de puntos clave del contrato (86afu5kej)\n- US-12 – Firmar digitalmente el contrato (86afu5kev)\n- US-13 – Confirmación de contrato firmado (86afu5key)\n\n### ÉPICA 4 – Gestión de pagos (86afu5k91)\n- US-14 – Pagar el canon desde la plataforma (86afu5kf0)\n- US-15 – Confirmación de pago al arrendador (86afu5ker)\n- US-16 – Consultar historial de pagos (86afu5kem)\n- US-17 – Generar reportes mensuales de ingresos (86afu5kf1)\n\n### ÉPICA 5 – Seguimiento del proceso (86afu5k8y)\n- US-18 – Visualizar estado del arriendo (86afu5keg)\n- US-19 – Recibir notificaciones del proceso (86afu5kex)\n\n## What to do\n\n1. For each user story / NFR task above, analyze the codebase to determine its implementation status. Look at:\n   - Backend modules: `src/backend/modules/` (controllers, use cases, repositories, DTOs)\n   - Frontend pages: `src/frontend/app/` (routes, components)\n   - Frontend modules: `src/frontend/modules/` (components, services)\n   - Kiro specs: `.kiro/specs/` (completed task lists)\n   - Database schema: `src/backend/db/prisma/schema.prisma`\n\n2. For each task, determine one of these statuses:\n   - ✅ Implementado — feature is fully implemented (backend + frontend)\n   - 🔧 En progreso — partial implementation exists (e.g. backend done but frontend pending, or spec exists with tasks in progress)\n   - ⏳ Pendiente — no implementation found yet\n\n3. For each task, post a comment on the ClickUp task using `clickup_create_task_comment` with:\n   - A brief status line (✅/🔧/⏳ + status label)\n   - A summary of what exists in the codebase (specific files/modules found)\n   - What's missing if not fully implemented\n   - Date of this analysis\n\n4. Also post a summary comment on the parent milestone task (86afu5ga8) with an overview table of all tasks and their statuses.\n\n## Status updates\n\nAfter analyzing each task, update its ClickUp status based on the implementation status:\n- ✅ Implementado → set ClickUp status to \"in review\"\n- 🔧 En progreso → set ClickUp status to \"in development\"\n- ⏳ Pendiente → set ClickUp status to \"scoping\"\n- Do NOT close or complete any task — never set status to \"done\", \"closed\", or \"complete\".\n\n### Allowed status transitions\n- Tasks in \"backlog\" → can move to \"scoping\", \"in development\", or \"in review\" based on analysis.\n- Tasks in \"scoping\" → can move to \"in development\" (if progress warrants it). Do NOT move backwards to \"backlog\".\n- Tasks in \"in development\" → can move to \"in review\" (if fully implemented). Do NOT move backwards to \"scoping\" or \"backlog\".\n- Tasks already in \"in review\", \"done\", \"closed\", or \"complete\" → do NOT change their status at all.\n- In summary: only forward transitions are allowed. Never regress a task's status.\n\n## Comment deduplication\n\nBefore posting a comment on a task, read the existing comments on that task using `clickup_get_task_comments`. Compare your current analysis against the most recent comment:\n- If the status (✅/🔧/⏳) and the summary of what exists / what's missing are essentially the same as the last comment, do NOT post a new comment — skip that task.\n- Only post a new comment if there is meaningful progress or a status change since the last comment.\n- This avoids cluttering tasks with repetitive identical updates.\n\n## Important rules\n- Be thorough: actually read the relevant code files to verify implementation, don't just check if files exist\n- Be concise in comments: keep each comment under 500 words\n- Write comments in Spanish (matching the task language)\n- Include the current date in each comment\n- Never close or complete tasks — map statuses as: Implementado → \"in review\", En progreso → \"in development\", Pendiente → \"scoping\"\n- Never regress a task's status — only move forward (backlog → scoping → in development → in review)"
  }
}